      "factual_description": "Jazz at Lincoln Center presents Gerry Mulligan Centennial: Mulligan and Me in The Appel Room on June 4-5, 2027, with Friday sets at 7:00 PM and 9:00 PM and Saturday sets at 4:30 PM and 7:00 PM. The work is conceived by writer Iris Dart and directed by Rachel Dart as a play with music about Mulligan's creative partnership with actress and singer Judy Holliday in the 1960s. Ted Nash, a longtime Mulligan collaborator and protégé, serves as music director, and current JLCO baritone saxophonist Paul Nedzela is featured.",
