        "en": {
          "why_it_matters": "The direct lineage is what makes this more than another centennial repertory night. Ted Nash worked with Mulligan and carries that language from inside the band, while Paul Nedzela puts a contemporary baritone voice next to it. Building the concert around Mulligan's creative relationship with Judy Holliday also opens a less familiar side of his history and turns the evening into a hybrid of live jazz, memory and theater rather than a museum-style tribute.",
